Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Phase=206.0:=20KEY2=20weak=20pull-up=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20un-stick=20first-boot=20reset?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AX301 has no external pull-up on the KEY2 input.  Without one, the pin
floats below the input threshold, so `rstn_int <= KEY2 and por_cnt(3)`
in ax301_top.vhd is permanently 0 — the NEORV32 CPU never comes out of
reset and stage2 produces no UART output.

First hit during Phase 6 silicon bring-up (2026-05-17): JTAG-loaded
host bitstream was silent on /dev/ttyUSB0 despite blinky / uart-blinker
test bitstreams running fine on the same board.  Bypassing KEY2 in RTL
(`rstn_int <= por_cnt(3)`) confirmed the root cause; this commit ships
the proper one-line QSF fix (internal Cyclone IV weak pull-up).

After the fix, listener-first JTAG SRAM load of the host bitstream
yields the expected boot trace:

    [stage2] ready - RV32IMAC NEORV32 loader
    [stage2] CLK=0x02faf080
    [stage2] SDRAM word-write test...
    [stage2] SDRAM test PASS
    [stage2] l=xmodem s=smoke d=dump w=wtest W=wmulti R=rdhdr B=baud …
    [stage2] CRTM locked — waiting for host command

(Listener must be open BEFORE openFPGALoader returns; stage2 drains the
boot burst then idles inside uart_getc_timeout(3600000) — opening cat
afterwards catches an idle line and looks like silence.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 quartus/neorv32_demo.qsf | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/quartus/neorv32_demo.qsf b/quartus/neorv32_demo.qsf
index a22f192..e849f54 100644
--- a/quartus/neorv32_demo.qsf
+++ b/quartus/neorv32_demo.qsf
@@ -90,6 +90,10 @@ set_global_assignment -name SDC_FILE neorv32_demo.sdc
 # ── Pin assignments (AX301 board) ────────────────────────────────────────────
 set_location_assignment PIN_E1  -to CLOCK
 set_location_assignment PIN_E16 -to KEY2
+# AX301 has no external pull-up on KEY2 — without this, the pin floats
+# low and rstn_int (KEY2 & por_cnt(3)) is wedged at 0, so the CPU is in
+# permanent reset (Phase 6 bring-up finding 2026-05-17).
+set_instance_assignment -name WEAK_PULL_UP_RESISTOR ON -to KEY2
 set_location_assignment PIN_M2  -to RXD
 set_location_assignment PIN_G1  -to TXD
 set_location_assignment PIN_G15 -to LED[0]
